        "density": 0.13417,
        "chars": 182,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 9.46
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        187,
        812,
        1489,
        962
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, the state of emergency to address the threat and impacts of COVID-19 in the\nCity of New York first declared in Emergency Executive Order No. 98, dated March 12, 2020,\nand extended most recently by Emergency Executive Order No. 315, dated January 20, 2023,\nremains in effect; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.2934,
          "min": -1.6116
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 84,
          "mean": -0.0047,
          "min": -0.3877
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 29490,
        "area_px": 191850,
        "density": 0.15371,
        "chars": 287,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 9.73
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        185,
        1005,
        1488,
        1117
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, this Order is given because of the propensity of the virus to spread person-to-person, and also because the actions taken to prevent such spread have led to property loss and damage; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2486,
          "min": -1.3029
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 39,
          "mean": -0.0138,
          "min": -0.4756
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 19874,
        "area_px": 143136,
        "density": 0.13885,
        "chars": 195,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 9.81
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        185,
        1159,
        1488,
        1312
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, Executive Order No. 25, dated February 6, 2023, rescinded the requirement\nfor prospective City employees to be vaccinated against COVID-19 as of February 10, 2023; and\non February 9, 2023, the Board of Health resolved to make COVID-19 vaccination optional for\ncertain City and DOE employees; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.23,
          "min": -1.4782
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 88,
          "mean": -0.0026,
          "min": -0.2263
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 31286,
        "area_px": 195534,
        "density": 0.16,
        "chars": 304,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 9.72
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        182,
        1352,
        1488,
        1575
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, pursuant to paragraph 6.2.6 of the Personnel Rules and Regulations of the\nCity of New York (\"PRR\"), a person who was dismissed from a permanent competitive or labor\nclass position in an agency under the jurisdiction of the Commissioner of Citywide Administrative\nServices may submit a written application for reinstatement in accordance with the Rule, and is\neligible for discretionary reinstatement for a period of one year only from the date of dismissal;\nand",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2147,
          "min": -1.2483
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
